This is a faceless cinematic journey in a fixed five-beat format (POV sprint + HAND opens the door + barge through, POV brief step to the top of stairs immediately inside, POV CONTINUOUS DESCENT, OFF-POV lateral tracking in the lower room, OFF-POV follow into another room). Honor the camera mode of this scene: scenes 1-3 are first-person POV (body-cam, body never visible except S1 forearms occasionally and the door-shoving hand at the very end of S1); scenes 4-5 are calm off-POV third-person, traveler seen only from behind or in profile, face never shown, clothing locked across S4 and S5. The structure's interior is a SMALL ENTRANCE LANDING with stairs going DOWN immediately inside the front door (not a room to walk across). Keep the locked structure identity through the exterior portions. The image must advance the journey only a believable short step from the previous keyframe. No on-screen text, numbers, logos, or watermarks. Single continuous frame only.

motion.prompt_template:
{kling_prompt}

This is a faceless cinematic journey in a fixed five-beat format. Honor the camera mode stated for this scene. SCENES 1-3 FIRST-PERSON POV (battered body-cam/handheld). Scene 1: BODY-CAM on a panicked sprinting runner FLEEING on a slightly non-linear path STRAIGHT AT the door (centered at 20–25m in K0) — EXTREME footstep bob, WORLD RUSHES PAST at sprint speed, per-stride SURGE-AND-SETTLE, NO FRAME IS STEADY (irregular jolts, stumble-recovers, water droplets / lens splash / motion blur in wet settings or dust / lens flare / motion blur in dry settings), 3–4 strides per second flat-out sprint, frame rotation 8–15 degrees per stride, panicked panting breath, door remains the dominant focal point, brief 1–2 shoulder-glances backward, forearms occasionally and briefly at the bottom of frame (NOT exaggerated), AND at the end the runner's HAND THRUSTS forward into the BOTTOM-CENTER of the frame (palm out, fingers extended, VISIBLY entering frame) and SHOVES the door open INWARD in one fast motion — the door YIELDS INWARD instantly under the VISIBLE HAND push (the door does NOT open by itself or automatically) — and the runner BARGES THROUGH without slowing into the structure FACING INTO it with the STAIRCASE GOING DOWN immediately visible ahead. Scene 2: a hurried brief 1–2-step POV walk forward to the top of the staircase, the camera angling DOWNWARD onto the descending steps. Scene 3: POV CONTINUOUS DESCENT down the staircase, camera STAYS POV start-to-end (NEVER lifts off the head, NEVER cuts, NEVER floats through stairs, NEVER passes through walls), angled DOWNWARD watching steps roll past, per-step bob downward, warm amber light grows brighter; THE FOOTSTEPS ON THE STAIRS ARE PROMINENT AND CLEARLY AUDIBLE — each step a distinct sound (timber creak / concrete thud / stone tap) DOMINATING the clip's audio. SCENES 4-5 OFF-POV THIRD-PERSON: calm controlled motion. Scene 4: a slow horizontal lateral tracking shot in the lower room while the traveler walks IN the room in ONE consistent forward direction (NOT on the staircase). Scene 5: a smooth continuous follow from behind as the traveler walks through into another luxurious room.

Keep the locked structure identity through the exterior portions. The descent is always a normal short straight step staircase going DOWN, structurally attached. The stairwell is fully enclosed with no outdoor window. Any handrail is on the side wall only. The audio is natural diegetic sound only — wind/sea/rain + HARD pounding footsteps on the SPECIFIC ground surface and panicked panting breath (S1, + hand-on-door SLAM and door creak/latch at end), brief footsteps on the SPECIFIC entrance-landing floor material (S2), PROMINENT AUDIBLE footsteps on the SPECIFIC stair material (S3, dominant audio), calm walking footsteps on the SPECIFIC lower-room floor material (S4-S5) — absolutely NO music. Every clip must depict ONE continuous motion from start to end.
